<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“See, that wasn’t so bad.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> laughs, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“I knew you’d win.”</span> You tell <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> that, despite that, some warning would have been nice. <span style="color:Pink">Being stripped and put on display like that isn’t exactly a friendly thing to do.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“No one saw your cock, except for me that is.”</span> He smirks, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“But you’re right. I apologize. It’s just a little game me and the boys play on new recruits, so to speak. Trust me, it could have been a lot worse.”</span> You still pout, rather not having to do something so embarrassing just to be accepted into his friend group. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Okay, okay. No need to cry.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> teases, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“How about, as a way to make it right, I tell you one embarrassing fact about me. But only if you agree to forgive me.”</span> You raise an eyebrow at this, not seeing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> as the type to do something like this. What’s in it for him? <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Just your forgiveness. I couldn’t bare to have you upset with me.”</span> He says genuinely, though his smirk clears you into the sarcasm. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Come on, this is rare opportunity. I wouldn’t tell this to just anyone, and neither will you, if you want to keep on living that it.”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You blush a little at his threat, thinking for a moment before agreeing.</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">You’re honestly curious what sort of embarrassing secret <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> could have.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Glad we could come to an agreement.”</span> He laughs, before his words turn a bit more seriously, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“But I meant what I said. One word of this to anyone and you’ll end up on the morning news. I’ll make sure it’s a very humiliating death.”</span> You chuckle nervously but get the idea he’s not kidding. You swear to not tell a soul. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Alright then.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Xavier</span> lets the silence linger for a secret before revealing this secret to you. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“When I was little, I used to have this big stuffed bear. Bigger than I was at the time. Sometimes, when I was alone, I used to play and pretended to have the bear punish me. Time-outs, scoldings, spankings, that sort of thing. I could count the number of times I got into real trouble on one hand, so I was curious what it was like. Nobody would ever see this, naturally, and I quickly grew out of it, but it was an interesting experience.”</span> <br>

